senses.gloss:
--(नृहरि and Narahari Narasimham (s.v.) half man and half lion अवतार् of विष्णु, worshipped as such in हरिवर्ष;
1: भा. II. 7. १४; V. १८. 7-१४; VII. 8. १५-16; X. 2. ४०; Vi. V. 5. १६.
came out of a post which हिरण्यकशिपु knocked with his fist; a description of his form and how he killed the demon;
2: भा. VII. 8. १५-31; XI. 4. १९.
still his anger was not appeased; praised by ब्रह्मा, Rudra, Indra, Sages, पितृस्, Siddhas, विद्याधरस्, नागस्, progenitors, Gandharvas, चारणस्, यक्षस्, Kimpuru- षस्, वैतालिकस्, Kinnaras, and विष्णु's attendants;
3: Ib. VII. 8. ३४ and ४०-56.
श्री was afraid to go near him;
4: Ib. VII. 9. 2.
at the request of the Gods प्रह्लाद praised the God for the welfare of the universe; offered boons to प्रह्लाद and advised him to rule his father's kingdom with his mind devoted to Hari until the time came for him to cast off his body;
5: Ib. V. १८. 7-१४; VI. 8. १४; VII. 9 (whole); १०. ११-14.
ब्रह्मा's praise of the Lord's disappearance.
6: Ib. VII. १०. २६-31; Br. III. ३३. २६.
God incarnate of विष्णु remembered by शिव for vanquishing मातृगण;
7: M. १७९. ४४-52, ७६.
created from out of his limbs a number of goddesses who overcame the Rudra, मातृगणस् and were blessed with divinity.
8: Ib. २४५. २१.
